# filee-bin repackages upstream's self-contained .NET/Avalonia release.
#
# The bundled native runtime (coreclr, Skia, PDFium, uiohook, the 7-Zip and
# rhwp engines) is built by upstream with its own hardening flags. This package
# deliberately does not patch or strip it (`options=(!strip)`), so the RELRO /
# PIE / "unstripped" warnings describe upstream artifacts, not a packaging
# mistake. Rebuilding them from source is not what this package is for.
#
# "Unused shared library" entries are the historic NEEDED stubs
# (libdl/libpthread/libm/librt/ld-linux) that glibc >= 2.34 folded into libc.
# They are harmless and removing them would mean patching upstream ELF files.
#
# The "included, but may not be needed" dependencies are loaded with dlopen,
# which namcap cannot see as an ELF edge:
#   * Avalonia's X11 backend: fontconfig, freetype2, libglvnd, libice, libsm,
#     libxcursor, libxext, libxfixes, libxi
#   * .NET runtime: icu, krb5, openssl, zlib
#   * engine downloads and update checks: ca-certificates
